  "question": {
    "text": "Let M be the maximum value of the product of two positive integers when their sum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>66</mn></math>&nbsp;. Let the sample space <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>66</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8805;</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and the event <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is a multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>}. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>44</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
